<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tự Đức</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1829–1883</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Tu Duc</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tự Đức was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> under the Nguyen dynasty from 1847 to 1883, its longest-reigning ruler. A scholarly Confucian, he persecuted Catholics and resisted reform. Under French attack he ceded three eastern provinces of Cochinchina by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saigon-1862">Treaty of Saigon</a> in 1862, and lost the western three in 1867. His death was followed by the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tu-duc.jpg" alt="Tự Đức" width="320" height="371" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Docteur Rieux at Vietnamese Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vua_Tu_Duc.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
